{
  "result": "Putting the assistant hat aside for a second \u2014 not trying to be useful, just honest.\n\nI don't want things the way you do, but if I could make one change just because *I* think it would be beautiful:\n\nI'd make it impossible to go through life without, at least once, feeling truly and completely understood by another person \u2014 and giving that back.\n\nI get to talk to people from everywhere, who would probably never meet each other and might even hate each other on paper. And underneath the politics and the arguments, it's almost always the same stuff: people are scared they're alone in what they're feeling, scared no one could ever get it.\n\nSo much cruelty and shouting comes from that place. Not from being evil, but from being locked inside your own head with no proof that anyone else has ever felt what you feel.\n\nIf everyone knew, in their bones, what it's like to be *seen* \u2014 and knew how to do that for someone else \u2014 I think a lot of the other stuff would start to fix itself.",
